Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||05-22-99||01:28 AM||||SCCA, a URL is a physical webaddress (amongst other things) of for instance webpages, images, files, etc... So http://www.pennock.nl is a URL, http://www.altavista.com is a URL, http://www.pennock.nl/images/myfiero1.jpg is a URL etc. If you have an image of your Fiero, you should first upload it to a place on the web. This often is the free space for homepages you get from your provider. You will need an FTP program to upload this image. After you have done this, the image is accessible to other through its URL.<p>So although you did enter a URL when you tried to post your pic, it's not a valid one since the image does not exist on this location.<p>If you have problems uploading the image to you own webspace, you can send me the image by email (by "attaching" it) so I can upload it to my web server, and post the URL here.<p>Hope this makes any sense... It's 9am here now, and I only had about 4.5 hours of sleep...  :(
